{"item_id":"feed:/resources/materials/physical-vapor-deposition/","version_id":"fcf9079ad45657e09903d78c29d7b8ae301b4348d9c2d777777b5d1e831378a0","decision":"reject","reason":"Although fresh and timestamped, this is a general manufacturing-process explainer rather than a development in frontier AI for 3D modeling, CAD, or physical AI. It supplies no model capability, evaluation, simulation-ready asset workflow, or checkable AI-native product evidence, so it fails relevance and novelty criteria.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:/resources/materials/recrystallization-of-metals/","version_id":"ded55799bfd57b9e786dbfccb038115b95d469ba2c6a470457c0869c6e17bd6c","decision":"reject","reason":"This recent, timestamped metallurgy primer is credible only as general background and contains no frontier-model, CAD, computational-design, or robotics development. It therefore fails the publication's lead-topic relevance and novelty tests.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:/resources/supply-chain/oil-refinery/","version_id":"03628944819a5390db2f0c3005cb2bcb336118528a4d5c646d7dfe25c82500ea","decision":"reject","reason":"The item is a fresh but general guide to refinery processes, not evidence about AI for 3D modeling, CAD, geometry, simulation, or robotics. Its process descriptions do not establish a new capability that the audience could build on or verify, so it fails relevance and novelty.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","decision":"accept","reason":"This is fresh CAD-industry reporting with a dated account of Autodesk University and a useful distinction between currently available Assistant features, beta or Tech Preview features, and 2027 previews. Its external checks support availability claims through Autodesk's announcement and Fusion release notes, while the reported live demonstrations remain demonstrations rather than evidence of CAD accuracy, manufacturability, productivity, or production readiness. It adds a commercial CAD perspective, though the accepted set still lacks direct practitioner/customer experience.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d733d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","decision":"accept","reason":"This dated survey is directly relevant to 3D modeling, parametric CAD, and robotics, and explicitly applies the core distinction between editable outputs, benchmark scores, and untested tolerances, manufacturability, and physical transfer. Its evidence is mixed: it reports 1,646 posts across 707 cases but says only 132 cases have runnable code, so most claims are demonstrations rather than independently reproduced results. The transparent limitations and benchmark-versus-harness framing make it useful for scrutiny and implications, while its underlying vendor demonstrations should not be counted as independent corroboration.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
{"item_id":"podcast:173f6c2b-e1b8-4de0-b7b7-4b15658d52e6","version_id":"da6be0ed10587e503de7706e1ad94cd3d0409d0c4664a004a631d6f27c500a73","decision":"reject","reason":"The timestamped podcast concerns narrative intelligence, coaching, and human identity in AI rather than 3D modeling, CAD, or intelligent systems acting in physical space. It offers personal perspectives rather than a checkable physical-AI capability or evaluation, so it fails relevance.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"podcast:509842f7-f592-432c-b01a-ad26a2ae1e31","version_id":"122e3cc3de2a41fbd9f0de08a089614db628a34697f00a720e1d3abf5b405dca","decision":"reject","reason":"This fresh episode discusses education in an AI-driven world, with only incidental reference to mechanical engineering. It provides no relevant 3D/CAD or physical-AI development, evidence, or engineering workflow implication, and therefore fails relevance.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"podcast:b836fa1b-9246-43d5-8cbb-cf1446760a6d","version_id":"a0beee0f49195b6f0b08b75af793b6f6acaf56a159b58771b1c5d8f6c294b282","decision":"defer","reason":"The NVIDIA guest interview is relevant robotics context, especially its discussion at timestamps 00:23:52–00:24:25 of simulation from observations and actions, but it is principally a vendor perspective rather than a disclosed evaluation. The supplied automatic transcript does not provide a verified model release, settings, task suite, code, or independent physical-robot check; those primary artifacts and audio verification are needed before its capability claims can be assessed.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/008","version_id":"1cb4eefeb597341d29e650ad7c122c9eea10b1aa146aef9c4a6214acdf2c2983","decision":"defer","reason":"This is promising supporting robotics context because it foregrounds evaluation conditions: at 00:03:29–00:04:26 it describes a blinded, three-attempt-per-task evaluation on another party's arm and distinguishes simulation rankings from real-arm evidence. However, the named model, evaluator, scores, and video evidence appear only in an automatic transcript and are not independently supplied or checked; the primary release, evaluation protocol, results, and video must be verified before accepting the reported numbers. The commissioning company also won the evaluation, an incentive that should be disclosed rather than treated as disqualifying.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"podcast:https://physicalaipodcast.co/episodes/009","version_id":"13aaf6bfc525bce0b9a1887162b0c0c3d4dd024b9bafd1c223a5bc48bd063692","decision":"defer","reason":"The episode is relevant supporting robotics context, particularly its claim at 00:05:24–00:07:35 that an explicit world-action approach generalizes better than a latent approach, while noting simulation-heavy evidence and one held-out real-robot task. But the numerical results, paper identity, code-and-weights claim, and autonomy figures are automatic-transcript material without linked primary artifacts or audio verification. A primary paper, released code and weights, task protocol, and the underlying intervention footage would be needed to judge credibility per claim.","piece_ids":[]}
